-Q</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hydbring</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dahlborn</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changes in plasma cortisol, plasma &#x003b2;-endorphin, heart rate, haematocrit and plasma protein concentration in horses during restraint and use of a naso-gastric tube</article-title><source>Pferdeheilkunde</source><year>1996</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>427</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lebelt</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Zanella</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Unshelm</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physiological correlates associated with cribbing behaviour in horses: changes in thermal threshold, heart rate, plasma beta-endorphin and serotonin</article-title><source>Equine vet J Suppl</source><year>1998</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10484999</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McGreevy</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicol</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physiological and behavioral consequences associated with short-term prevention of crib-biting in horses</article-title><source>Physiol Behav</source><year>1998</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>23</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9811360</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0031-9384(98)00070-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><sur